WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.370
- Tons and tons of people are upset

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.880
that the COVID relief bill

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.840
has a bunch of extra spending in it.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.820
Pork barrel spending on things
unrelated to COVID relief.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.750
Why should a COVID bill have earmarks

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:12.790
for higher education and foreign aid?

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:13.623
It doesn't make sense.

00:00:13.623 --> 00:00:14.990
Well, it actually does

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.060
because this isn't really a COVID bill,

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.360
for various procedural reasons
I'm not going to go into,

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.040
this is actually a spending bill

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.930
that happens to have a
COVID bill attached to it.

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:26.240
This is a bill that
funds the U.S. government

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.316
through September of 2021.

00:00:28.316 --> 00:00:30.810
$1.4 trillion to keep
the government running.

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:32.770
And for various arcane procedural reasons,

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:36.610
it made sense to add the $900
million COVID relief bill

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:39.300
onto the $1.4 trillion spending bill.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.650
So this isn't a COVID bill
with a bunch of extra spending.

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.820
It's a spending bill with a
bunch of extra COVID stuff.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:45.550
And if you'd like even
more legal analysis,

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:46.820
check out my real law reviews

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:49.140
where I tackle all the
legal news of the day,

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.003
and I'll see you in court.

